{"hash":"d5357ec691fcea29","voice":"en-IN-NeerjaExpressiveNeural","rate":"+4%","dur":84.61,"said":"Om Namah Shivaya. Come, walk with me. Stand here a moment at the top of the steps, and breathe. You are on the crest of the Sahyadri, the Western Ghats, about nine hundred metres up, and all around you is forest, thick and green and often wrapped in mist. Since 1985 these hills have been the Bhimashankar Wildlife Sanctuary, about a hundred and thirty square kilometres, set aside above all for one shy animal: the Indian giant squirrel, the shekru, Maharashtra’s state animal. Look up into the high branches; a long, dark tail might be hanging down. Before the monsoon, the temple trust says, thousands of fireflies light up the village at night. Now look down, past the shops. Far below, in a green hollow, stands a small black-stone temple. That hollow is where the river Bhima is born, the river that crosses the Deccan and, at Pandharpur, is called the Chandrabhaga. The Lord who lives there shares her name: Bhimashankar. And the Shiva Purana says these mountains were once home to a very different Bhima. Let us go down the steps together, and I will tell you about him.\n\nDid you know? From Kokan Kada, a cliff near the village, the land drops about three thousand feet to the Konkan plain below.","segments":[{"key":"text","start":0,"end":1078},{"key":"didYouKnow","start":1094,"end":1204}],"words":[[0.098,0.204,0,2],[0.314,0.312,3,8],[0.639,0.553,9,16],[2.127,0.433,18,22],[2.728,0.312,24,28],[3.053,0.204,29,33],[3.269,0.288,34,36],[4.423,0.421,38,43],[4.856,0.24,44,48],[5.108,0.036,49,50],[5.156,0.541,51,57],[5.709,0.096,58,60],[5.817,0.096,61,64],[5.926,0.276,65,68],[6.214,0.084,69,71],[6.31,0.096,72,75],[6.418,0.493,76,81],[7.019,0.204,83,86],[7.236,0.445,87,94],[8.594,0.192,96,99],[8.798,0.12,100,103],[8.93,0.108,104,106],[9.05,0.084,107,110],[9.147,0.361,111,116],[9.519,0.084,117,119],[9.615,0.096,120,123],[9.724,0.685,124,132],[10.625,0.144,134,137],[10.781,0.421,138,145],